<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan gold rates seen mixed before elections.</title>
<headline>Pakistan gold rates seen mixed before elections.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan gold rates are likely to remain mixed amid subdued demand for jewellery before the February 3 general elections, dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Demand for jewellery has fallen before the elections,&quot; one dealer said, without elaborating.</p>
<p>Silver rates remained stable last week, the dealer said.</p>
<p>    Gold 24 carat in rupees per 10 grammes Sunday   Jan 13</p>
<p>							 5,082    5,138</p>
<p>    Silver per 1,000 grammes		   7,715    7,715</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees)</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
